&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span&gt;Type System&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The following subclasses are used in conjunction with standard classes (&lt;em&gt;e.g.&lt;/em&gt; Safe // Location) to denote the applicable method of containment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;wiki-content-table&quot;&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Class&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Definition&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Appearances&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Location&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Item requires containment to be built around it.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;PENDING ASSIGNMENT&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Object&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Item does not need containment built around its position and does not have containment procedures which are reactionary.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2156&quot;&gt;SCP-2156&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Phenomenon&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Item has containment procedures which are reactionary in nature.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1422&quot;&gt;SCP-1422&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5107&quot;&gt;SCP-5107&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span&gt;Object/Containment System&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
